    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e78816e_967fecf8",
        "filename": "core/res/AndroidManifest.xml",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1004,
      "author": {
        "id": 1034265
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-11-22T03:34:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wonder if we really need separate permissions for READ_PHONE_STATE and READ_PRECISE_PHONE_STATE. It\u0027s a pretty subtle distinction and probably not one that makes sense to end users?",
      "revId": "363ba26d67734701f5017109913b2053a408eb99",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "835dfa61_19dc4bfe",
        "filename": "core/res/AndroidManifest.xml",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1004,
      "author": {
        "id": 1021495
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-11-27T15:57:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We consider appropriate to make a distinction between the old events with the information they currently expose and the new ones that offer a finer coarse info about the phone/data connection events.\nSome users should be aware of the new information gathered by the apps when the update goes live.\nAnyway, we understand the overload of having a new permission with the effort of maintaining all the translations and so on, so if you consider appropriate to merge it with the existing one it could be ok too.",
      "parentUuid": "1e78816e_967fecf8",
      "revId": "363ba26d67734701f5017109913b2053a408eb99",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e8fa1ae_a123b839",
        "filename": "services/java/com/android/server/TelephonyRegistry.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 606,
      "author": {
        "id": 1034265
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-11-22T03:34:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the \"precise\" data connection changed event can be delivered through onPreciseDataConnectionStateChanged then it would be logical to deliver the existing event through onDataConnectionStateChanged. I guess we can\u0027t change that, though.",
      "revId": "363ba26d67734701f5017109913b2053a408eb99",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6352c652_1801e595",
        "filename": "services/java/com/android/server/TelephonyRegistry.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 606,
      "author": {
        "id": 1021495
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-11-27T15:57:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using onDataConnectionStateChanged we cannot obtain the DataConnection fail event because it does not provide any fail reason.",
      "parentUuid": "1e8fa1ae_a123b839",
      "revId": "363ba26d67734701f5017109913b2053a408eb99",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e8fa1ae_61fb7060",
        "filename": "services/java/com/android/server/TelephonyRegistry.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 881,
      "author": {
        "id": 1034265
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-11-22T03:34:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should this and the other newly added broadcasts be sticky?",
      "revId": "363ba26d67734701f5017109913b2053a408eb99",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6352c652_780621af",
        "filename": "services/java/com/android/server/TelephonyRegistry.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 881,
      "author": {
        "id": 1021495
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-11-27T15:57:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We created those broadcast like the existing one on TelephonyManager.broadcastCallStateChanged which is not sticky.\nAlso it is not so clear for us if the sticky broadcast does the permission check to ensure the app has requested the READ_PRECISE_PHONE_STATE/READ_PHONE_STATE permission.",
      "parentUuid": "1e8fa1ae_61fb7060",
      "revId": "363ba26d67734701f5017109913b2053a408eb99",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
