    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e78816e_d6a2444c",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/PreciseCallState.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 142,
      "author": {
        "id": 1034265
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-11-22T03:34:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The values defined in CallFailCause.java are not in ril.h so can/will the RIL actually use them?",
      "revId": "363ba26d67734701f5017109913b2053a408eb99",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6352c652_b8ef199a",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/PreciseCallState.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 142,
      "author": {
        "id": 1021495
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-11-27T15:57:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As per comments on ril.h, the RIL implementation can return other exact cause codes despite of they are not defined on ril.h.\n\"* If the implementation does not have access to the exact cause codes,\n * then it should return one of the values listed in RIL_LastCallFailCause,\n * as the UI layer needs to distinguish these cases for tone generation or\n * error notification.\"\n \nAlso we have observed that vendor implementation of RIL often use codes not listed neither in ril.h nor CallFailCause.java, even out of value range defined in the 3GPP TS 24.008\nSo our intention is to propagate the exact code returned by RIL implementation to the app level so the developers can use them discretionally.",
      "parentUuid": "1e78816e_d6a2444c",
      "revId": "363ba26d67734701f5017109913b2053a408eb99",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
